1
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:11,967
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:32,067 --> 00:00:33,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,267
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,100
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:44,133
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:45,300
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,433
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,267
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:53,467
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:55,433
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,633 --> 00:00:58,133
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,133 --> 00:01:00,267
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:02,767
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:06,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:11,667
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:13,167
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,167 --> 00:01:14,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:22,833
<i> Why are you insisting
on settling anyway?</i>

21
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,533
<i>Maybe you already
got something.</i>

22
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:25,567
<i> It doesn't matter.</i>

23
00:01:25,567 --> 00:01:28,300
<i>You're putting
Ginintuang Lupa in danger.</i>

24
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:31,633
<i>Ginintuang Lupa has
always been in danger.</i>

25
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:33,467
<i> This isn't our land!</i>

26
00:01:33,467 --> 00:01:36,633
So as long as they want to give,
<i> I'll accept it.</i>

27
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:39,467
<i> Integrity, intelligence,
capability...</i>

28
00:01:39,467 --> 00:01:42,300
<i> ...and a heart that beats
for others.</i>

29
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:46,200
<i>Those will be the keys
for Gabo to succeed</i>

30
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,833
<i> in his next missions.</i>

31
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:49,367
<i> Gabo is the fire...</i>

32
00:01:49,367 --> 00:01:52,233
<i>...that will burn
for the salvation of the masses.</i>

33
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:53,233
<i> I'm going home.</i>

34
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:55,067
<i>I'm no use here anyway.
I'm suspended.</i>

35
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:57,667
<i> I'll just wait
</i>for Internal Affairs' decision.

36
00:01:57,667 --> 00:01:59,867
<i>Boss. We're only going
after a woman.</i>

37
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:01,533
<i> Why do we have many weapons?</i>

38
00:02:01,533 --> 00:02:04,067
<i>I'll make sure this is
her last trip.</i>

39
00:02:04,067 --> 00:02:06,367
<i> Let's finish Samantha Jacinto
tonight.</i>

40
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:08,633
[GABO] Pa.

41
00:02:09,367 --> 00:02:10,400
What happened?

42
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,833
Why is Aunt Betchay upset again?

43
00:02:11,833 --> 00:02:15,200
Oh dear, she even has
the nerve to be angry.

44
00:02:15,233 --> 00:02:16,567
[DANTE] You see, Betchay...

45
00:02:16,567 --> 00:02:19,533
...has been talking to someone
who wants your father to settle.

46
00:02:19,533 --> 00:02:21,100
[MAMENG]
She's already been bought.

47
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,133
Paid off.

48
00:02:22,133 --> 00:02:24,367
Rudy won't get any peace
from her.

49
00:02:24,633 --> 00:02:25,700
What settlement?

50
00:02:26,433 --> 00:02:28,133
No one's going to settle!

51
00:02:28,133 --> 00:02:30,700
Pa, whoever shot you
should go to jail!

52
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,700
That's exactly what I'm saying!

53
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:35,600
But your Aunt Betchay
is stubborn!

54
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,600
Wait, can all of you just
stop worrying about that?

55
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,100
Because no matter what happens,

56
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:40,700
I'll never agree
to a settlement!

57
00:02:41,133 --> 00:02:43,367
[DANTE] There, Rudy has made
his decision.

58
00:02:43,733 --> 00:02:46,367
Let Betchay rant all she wants.

59
00:02:46,367 --> 00:02:47,300
[MAMENG] Right.

60
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:48,733
Gabo hasn't eaten yet.

61
00:02:48,767 --> 00:02:50,500
Come on, Gabo.
The food is ready.

62
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,433
Let's have dinner together.

63
00:02:52,433 --> 00:02:53,600
[GABO] What do they think?

64
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,233
Not everyone can be bribed
with money!

65
00:02:55,233 --> 00:02:56,400
That's right!

66
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,567
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

67
00:02:57,567 --> 00:02:58,567
[MAMENG] Come on.

68
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,633
[BETCHAY, IN SINGSONG VOICE]
Hello!

69
00:03:01,633 --> 00:03:02,633
Good evening!

70
00:03:02,633 --> 00:03:04,400
Why are you all outside?

71
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,300
Tonight has been so slow!
No customers!

72
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:07,800
Oh, it's just too early.

73
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,500
But I'm here now!

74
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,433
Don't you worry!

75
00:03:11,433 --> 00:03:12,433
Come on.

76
00:03:12,433 --> 00:03:14,267
- Let's go inside.
- Right.

77
00:03:14,267 --> 00:03:15,733
Someone's full of hot air
out here.

78
00:03:15,733 --> 00:03:17,767
- Say what now?
- Look at these two.

79
00:03:17,767 --> 00:03:18,600
Go on!

80
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:21,400
You two, follow along!
Get inside!

81
00:03:21,433 --> 00:03:22,667
- Betchay.
- Go ahead.

82
00:03:22,667 --> 00:03:24,300
Come on. You too, Betchay.

83
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:26,333
- Let's go.
- Later. I'll drum up business.

84
00:03:26,333 --> 00:03:27,833
- I'll get some customers.
- Okay.

85
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:29,267
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:03:29,267 --> 00:03:30,467
Psst! Hey, you two!

87
00:03:30,467 --> 00:03:32,600
Want to come inside for a beer?

88
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:34,467
Snobs.

89
00:03:34,467 --> 00:03:35,700
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING
IN DISTANCE]

90
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:36,833
Come on-- Hey!

91
00:03:36,833 --> 00:03:38,300
There you are!

92
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:39,433
- [MAN 1] Whoa, dude.
- [GIGGLES]

93
00:03:39,433 --> 00:03:40,633
- She's beautiful.
- Come on in!

94
00:03:40,633 --> 00:03:42,933
Let's go inside
and have a drink!

95
00:03:42,933 --> 00:03:44,367
- What do you say? Come on!
- Really?

96
00:03:44,367 --> 00:03:46,167
- Are you sure?
- Come on, follow me!

97
00:03:46,167 --> 00:03:48,467
- Let's go! This way!
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:50,733
It's cheap here! Come along!

99
00:03:51,433 --> 00:03:52,867
So, one bucket of beer?

100
00:03:52,867 --> 00:03:54,767
- Just one bottle each.
- For both of you?

101
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,400
How about you add some snacks?

102
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,200
Maybe crackers? Sounds good?

103
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:00,333
- As long as you'll sit here.
- Of course we'll sit together!

104
00:04:00,333 --> 00:04:01,500
[MAN 2] Then let's have
some beers and crackers!

105
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:02,800
Here we go!

106
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,867
Another bottle?

107
00:04:03,867 --> 00:04:05,400
- You can't--
- Let me through!

108
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,833
- [MAN 3] Hey, Betchay!
- Oh!

109
00:04:06,833 --> 00:04:08,000
Let's sit over there
for a drink!

110
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,233
- Hang on!
- Stop right there!

111
00:04:09,233 --> 00:04:11,233
It's my turn now!
I've waited outside for ages!

112
00:04:11,233 --> 00:04:13,367
- Just for her!
- Wait! Wait a minute!

113
00:04:13,367 --> 00:04:17,233
Boys, it's too early to be
at each other's throats.

114
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:18,900
I have an idea.

115
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:21,900
How about the three of us
share the same table?

116
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,067
No, it's my turn now!

117
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:25,333
- I've waited long enough!
- Come on, boys.

118
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:27,467
It's all about the positioning.

119
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,600
Sit over there.

120
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,533
- Damn it.
- We were here first!

121
00:04:30,533 --> 00:04:32,233
- Yes, yes.
- I've waited for so long!

122
00:04:32,233 --> 00:04:34,600
[BETCHAY] Look, I'll sit here
in the middle.

123
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,233
Ask her!
She knows we were here first!

124
00:04:36,233 --> 00:04:38,433
- But I've waited forever!
- Let's hold hands together.

125
00:04:38,433 --> 00:04:40,567
Three customers at one table.

126
00:04:40,567 --> 00:04:41,900
- [BOTTLES CLINKING]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

127
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:43,833
- [WHOOPING]
- [MUSIC ENDS]

128
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:45,800
[BINOY PANTING]

129
00:04:46,667 --> 00:04:47,733
Are we clear?

130
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:49,900
We'll act like
we're Django's crew.

131
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:51,367
We've got to convince him.

132
00:04:51,367 --> 00:04:52,933
- We can't let him catch on.
- I wonder what's next for Gabo.

133
00:04:52,933 --> 00:04:54,867
- All that secrecy--
- [BINOY] What if Gabo finds out

134
00:04:54,867 --> 00:04:56,533
- Come on!
- ...we're Django's men again?

135
00:04:56,533 --> 00:04:59,367
- Hey! I knew it!
- What are you talking about?

136
00:04:59,367 --> 00:05:01,733
- [DABOY, BINOY] Ouch!
- You three couldn't be trusted!

137
00:05:01,767 --> 00:05:05,033
We welcomed you to the group,
yet this is how you repay us?

138
00:05:05,033 --> 00:05:06,967
- [TOLITS] N-No, no, no!
- [BONG] You bastards.

139
00:05:06,967 --> 00:05:09,400
You got it all wrong!
Let us explain!

140
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,367
- We can explain this!
- No! Absolutely not!

141
00:05:11,367 --> 00:05:13,367
- You'll explain this to Gabo!
- Come on, you traitors!

142
00:05:13,367 --> 00:05:14,733
- Wait a minute!
- Start walking!

143
00:05:14,733 --> 00:05:16,567
- It's a big misunderstanding!
- You're hurting me!

144
00:05:16,567 --> 00:05:18,067
- Ouch, ouch!
- We've been good to you!

145
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:19,400
[MUSIC ENDS]

146
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:21,367
[UTENSILS CLINKING, SCRAPING]

147
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:25,033
Gabo, how was your day?

148
00:05:28,867 --> 00:05:30,367
Uh, it was fine, Pa.

149
00:05:31,767 --> 00:05:32,833
You see...

150
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,767
Earlier, I...

151
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:38,400
...got an advance at work.

152
00:05:39,467 --> 00:05:40,800
But on the way,

153
00:05:41,333 --> 00:05:43,967
I passed by a mother and child
who were being robbed.

154
00:05:45,067 --> 00:05:47,033
The mother was shot, so...

155
00:05:47,567 --> 00:05:49,567
I brought her and the child
to the hospital.

156
00:05:49,567 --> 00:05:52,067
Oh no, I already know
how this story ends.

157
00:05:52,767 --> 00:05:54,300
You paid for it.

158
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:55,467
You helped them with the bill.

159
00:05:55,467 --> 00:05:57,600
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:00,367
[MAMENG] Well, do you have
some money left, Gabo?

161
00:06:01,067 --> 00:06:03,733
I still have something,
at least.

162
00:06:03,733 --> 00:06:06,067
It must have cost you a lot.

163
00:06:06,067 --> 00:06:07,300
[DANTE] Goodness.

164
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,733
If Betchay were here,
she would've scolded you.

165
00:06:09,767 --> 00:06:10,800
[MAMENG CHUCKLES]

166
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,933
Mameng.

167
00:06:12,433 --> 00:06:14,367
We're talking about
a person's life here.

168
00:06:14,367 --> 00:06:15,467
[MAMENG] Rudy...

169
00:06:15,467 --> 00:06:21,767
Dante doesn't take
Gabo's kindness for granted.

170
00:06:21,767 --> 00:06:23,000
The problem is,

171
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,633
we also have needs at home.

172
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:27,667
Just look up.

173
00:06:27,667 --> 00:06:29,700
The roof is leaking again.

174
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:33,800
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

175
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:34,933
Gabo.

176
00:06:35,967 --> 00:06:39,900
What I'm saying is that
maybe sometimes...

177
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,633
you should put family first

178
00:06:43,033 --> 00:06:44,967
Instead of other people.

179
00:06:45,967 --> 00:06:47,100
You know what?

180
00:06:48,167 --> 00:06:50,367
Both of you sound exactly
like Betchay.

181
00:06:51,367 --> 00:06:54,367
Gabo did the right thing,
yet you still criticize him.

182
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:56,733
Gabo didn't do anything wrong.

183
00:06:56,733 --> 00:06:58,500
What matters is that...

184
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:00,067
he saved someone's life.

185
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:02,900
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

186
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:03,967
You see...

187
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:05,800
Auntie...

188
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,700
I know I have obligations
here at home.

189
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,867
I just couldn't bear
to leave the child.

190
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:17,367
I didn't want him
to go through...

191
00:07:18,867 --> 00:07:20,367
the same things I did.

192
00:07:23,767 --> 00:07:25,033
Gabo.

193
00:07:25,033 --> 00:07:26,367
It's just money.

194
00:07:27,033 --> 00:07:28,700
It'll come back double.

195
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:31,633
- What's wrong?
- N-Nothing. It's no big deal.

196
00:07:33,933 --> 00:07:35,600
- We're not bad people!
- Shut up!

197
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,100
- How dare you!
- Come on now!

198
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:38,533
I was right!

199
00:07:38,533 --> 00:07:40,533
- You couldn't be trusted!
- You don't have to drag me!

200
00:07:40,533 --> 00:07:42,200
- I'm not a kid!
- [TEKLA] Gabo!

201
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,767
[TEKLA] Come outside, Gabo!

202
00:07:43,767 --> 00:07:44,967
[MAMENG] What's that?

203
00:07:45,667 --> 00:07:47,833
[DANTE] That must be
Gabo's friends again.

204
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,067
- Pa, excuse me.
- Sure thing.

205
00:07:50,067 --> 00:07:53,433
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

206
00:07:53,433 --> 00:07:55,767
[FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

207
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,400
[TEKLA] You have some
explaining to do...

208
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,900
- [BINOY] Stop it!
- ...and you'd better start now!

209
00:07:59,467 --> 00:08:00,500
Why?

210
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:03,700
Ask these three traitors, Gabo!

211
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:06,133
They're back to working
with Django again!

212
00:08:06,133 --> 00:08:07,733
- [DABOY] No, no, no!
- [TOLITS] Oh, come on!

213
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:09,567
Please, hear us out!

214
00:08:09,567 --> 00:08:12,133
It's not like we wanted to be
ambushed by Django and his crew.

215
00:08:12,133 --> 00:08:13,500
[TEKLA SCOFFS]

216
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,667
- You were ambushed? Why?
- [DABOY] Yeah.

217
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:17,133
Well, you see...

218
00:08:17,133 --> 00:08:18,800
He told us to spy on you.

219
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,900
Also, he wanted to know
where you get your money.

220
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,533
[BONG] See? That makes you
traitors, you bastards!

221
00:08:23,567 --> 00:08:25,067
[BINOY] No! For crying out loud!

222
00:08:25,067 --> 00:08:26,933
[IPE] What, did you betray Gabo?

223
00:08:26,933 --> 00:08:28,600
- [BINOY, DABOY] Huh?
- [TEKLA] Speak!

224
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:30,500
We'll never do that to Gabo!

225
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,233
We're on his side!

226
00:08:32,233 --> 00:08:34,933
[TOLITS] Yeah.
Then they dragged us away.

227
00:08:35,633 --> 00:08:36,567
Swear on your life?

228
00:08:36,567 --> 00:08:38,000
- [TOLITS, DABOY] Yeah!
- Of course!

229
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,567
[DABOY]
You just won't believe us!

230
00:08:39,967 --> 00:08:42,767
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]
- [DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:08:42,767 --> 00:08:43,933
[LUCAS] Well, Samantha?

232
00:08:43,933 --> 00:08:45,733
Still alive, huh?

233
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:54,000
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

234
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:01,033
[GUNSHOTS]

235
00:09:06,533 --> 00:09:09,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,667
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING]
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]

237
00:09:11,667 --> 00:09:12,600
[MAGAZINE CLICKING]

238
00:09:13,833 --> 00:09:16,500
[GUNSHOTS]

239
00:09:19,933 --> 00:09:21,600
[GUNSHOTS]

240
00:09:22,633 --> 00:09:25,700
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

241
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:30,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

242
00:09:30,967 --> 00:09:31,967
[GUNSHOTS]

243
00:09:33,567 --> 00:09:40,533
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

244
00:09:45,533 --> 00:09:52,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:57,667
She got away!

246
00:09:57,667 --> 00:10:00,000
[LAO] She won't get far, boss.
She's wounded.

247
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[LEE] Come on!

248
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,233
Let's go back to the car!

249
00:10:02,267 --> 00:10:03,533
Let's find her!

250
00:10:04,333 --> 00:10:05,333
Move it!

251
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:08,033
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

252
00:10:08,033 --> 00:10:09,200
[CAR DOORS OPENING]

253
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:12,733
[ENGINES REVVING]

254
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,833
As you can see, Romy,
Django's really smart!

255
00:10:19,767 --> 00:10:24,200
He's now befriending
Gabo's friends...

256
00:10:24,933 --> 00:10:27,067
...so he could get information.

257
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,800
But maybe it's the opposite
that'll happen.

258
00:10:33,667 --> 00:10:35,667
They wouldn't dare cross Django.

259
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:36,667
[ROMY CHUCKLES]

260
00:10:39,033 --> 00:10:40,033
Look, it's Betchay!

261
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:42,967
[PAQUITO EXHALES]

262
00:10:42,967 --> 00:10:46,600
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

263
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,733
- Betchay!
- Oh, sir!

264
00:10:48,733 --> 00:10:51,700
Can I talk to you
for a moment?

265
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,200
- Oh!
- [MAN] But Paquito,

266
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:55,800
you can clearly see
Betchay's with us right now.

267
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:57,267
We're still talking to her.

268
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,000
Get it?

269
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:05,900
- What if I ban you in here?
- Oh, no. Yes, we can talk.

270
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:08,633
I'll be back. I'll be back.
Let's sit over there.

271
00:11:08,667 --> 00:11:15,600
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

272
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:24,567
[RUDY] Forgive me, son.

273
00:11:25,167 --> 00:11:29,200
<i>I shouldn't have let myself
be tempted to gamble again.</i>

274
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:32,633
<i>I know you worked hard
for that money.</i>

275
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,400
<i> And we do need that money.</i>

276
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,867
<i> But I'm a weak man.</i>

277
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:40,967
<i> I'm easily tempted.</i>

278
00:11:41,933 --> 00:11:45,100
<i>No matter how many times
I said I wouldn't do it again...</i>

279
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:48,167
<i> in just one instance...</i>

280
00:11:49,367 --> 00:11:51,800
<i> I forgot my promise.</i>

281
00:11:54,933 --> 00:11:58,300
<i> I hope you can forgive me.</i>

282
00:12:00,167 --> 00:12:07,133
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

283
00:12:09,367 --> 00:12:11,033
Gabo, what do we do?

284
00:12:11,033 --> 00:12:13,767
Django thinks
we're his men again.

285
00:12:13,767 --> 00:12:19,267
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

286
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:20,867
Are these guys saying the truth?

287
00:12:20,867 --> 00:12:22,367
- Yeah.
- Yeah! It's true, Gabo.

288
00:12:24,333 --> 00:12:25,367
If you...

289
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:28,000
cross me again...

290
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:30,367
...you know
what can happen to you.

291
00:12:30,367 --> 00:12:31,700
Do you understand?

292
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:33,100
- Yes, Gabo.
- Yes, Gabo, we know.

293
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,133
Here's what you'll do.

294
00:12:35,967 --> 00:12:39,800
Make Django believe
you're on his side.

295
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,933
You'll be my eyes and ears
in their group.

296
00:12:44,867 --> 00:12:47,233
Find out what he's planning
against me.

297
00:12:47,233 --> 00:12:48,333
Is that clear?

298
00:12:48,367 --> 00:12:49,433
- Yes, Gabo.
- Yes, Gabo.

299
00:12:49,433 --> 00:12:51,967
Gabo, are you sure
about this?

300
00:12:53,833 --> 00:12:57,867
[TOLITS] So, Gabo,
we're like your sky.

301
00:12:58,700 --> 00:12:59,933
- "Sky"?
- "Sky"?

302
00:12:59,933 --> 00:13:01,433
What "sky" are
you talking about?

303
00:13:01,433 --> 00:13:03,900
- What are you, heaven?
- No, "sky", like--

304
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:05,700
Like you're working
for the enemy,

305
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,000
but you're actually an ally.

306
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,067
- Spy!
- Then it's spy!

307
00:13:09,067 --> 00:13:10,900
- Did you have to slap me?
- [BONG] Gabo.

308
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,133
You think we can still trust
these guys?

309
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:17,467
Who else would I trust
with my back...

310
00:13:18,867 --> 00:13:19,967
...if not you?

311
00:13:21,733 --> 00:13:23,000
Here's what you'll do.

312
00:13:24,067 --> 00:13:28,000
You'll make Django believe
you're loyal to him.

313
00:13:28,967 --> 00:13:32,900
But if you feel
like things are looking bad,

314
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:34,167
come here at once.

315
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:39,533
I'll make sure he doesn't get
out of here alive.

316
00:13:39,533 --> 00:13:41,367
[STIRRING MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

317
00:13:41,367 --> 00:13:42,333
Alright, Gabo.

318
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:48,733
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

319
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:51,400
- Rudy.
- Oh.

320
00:13:52,367 --> 00:13:55,400
We'll clean
your wounds, alright?

321
00:13:56,567 --> 00:13:58,367
[GROANS] Oh, my.

322
00:14:03,233 --> 00:14:05,033
No, I'll do it myself, Mameng.

323
00:14:06,233 --> 00:14:08,967
Why? Can you see that clearly?

324
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:10,433
I'll do it. Come on.

325
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,733
Come on.

326
00:14:15,833 --> 00:14:17,067
Oh!

327
00:14:17,067 --> 00:14:21,300
Why is your wound that bad?
It's swelling and bruising!

328
00:14:22,167 --> 00:14:24,733
Why is it like that?
Are you out of medicine?

329
00:14:26,467 --> 00:14:31,133
We need to go to the hospital,
so they can check that.

330
00:14:31,167 --> 00:14:33,333
- Just wait. Gabo!
- Mameng. Don't.

331
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:35,967
Don't tell it to Gabo.

332
00:14:35,967 --> 00:14:39,400
Your health is
at stake here, Rudy.

333
00:14:40,133 --> 00:14:42,833
Why don't you want
Gabo to know?

334
00:14:42,833 --> 00:14:43,833
Um...

335
00:14:45,133 --> 00:14:47,400
Gabo already gave me money.

336
00:14:48,933 --> 00:14:50,800
But I didn't buy my medicine.

337
00:14:51,367 --> 00:14:52,333
Why?

338
00:14:53,467 --> 00:14:54,800
[RUDY SIGHS]

339
00:14:57,933 --> 00:14:59,400
I gambled and lost.

340
00:15:00,933 --> 00:15:03,367
I thought I could double
the money.

341
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,967
My gosh, Rudy!

342
00:15:05,467 --> 00:15:08,267
You're back to gambling?!

343
00:15:09,967 --> 00:15:11,133
It's not like that.

344
00:15:11,133 --> 00:15:16,167
It's like you don't know
what gambling did to your life.

345
00:15:16,167 --> 00:15:19,033
That destroyed
your family's future, remember?

346
00:15:19,467 --> 00:15:21,400
You lost Belinda!

347
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:24,500
What, do you want
to lose Gabo, too?

348
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,167
I was just tempted.

349
00:15:27,133 --> 00:15:28,633
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

350
00:15:28,633 --> 00:15:30,967
I won't cover up for you, Rudy.

351
00:15:32,967 --> 00:15:33,933
[MAMENG] Gabo!

352
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:38,033
Gabo. Can I have some money?

353
00:15:38,033 --> 00:15:41,067
It's for your father's medicine.
His wound's swelling.

354
00:15:42,933 --> 00:15:46,567
Auntie, I already gave Papa
money for his medicine.

355
00:15:46,567 --> 00:15:50,167
But that's the thing.
He lost it while gambling!

356
00:15:50,167 --> 00:15:52,400
What I don't understand
about your father

357
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:55,333
is how he could go back
to gambling in this situation!

358
00:15:55,333 --> 00:15:57,233
Papa used the money
for gambling?

359
00:15:57,233 --> 00:15:58,867
That's why I'm furious!

360
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,933
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

361
00:16:01,933 --> 00:16:03,167
He's in a bad mood again.

362
00:16:04,067 --> 00:16:05,067
[GABO] Pa.

363
00:16:06,333 --> 00:16:07,567
Is auntie saying the truth?

364
00:16:08,367 --> 00:16:10,167
The money I gave
for your medicine...

365
00:16:10,633 --> 00:16:13,533
- You used it for gambling?
- Gabo, I'm sorry.

366
00:16:13,533 --> 00:16:15,367
I was just hopeful.

367
00:16:15,367 --> 00:16:18,200
I thought I could double
the money you gave.

368
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,367
Pa, why did you do that?!

369
00:16:19,367 --> 00:16:22,533
[MAMENG] And how has
gambling ever helped you, huh?

370
00:16:22,533 --> 00:16:24,133
And you, too!

371
00:16:24,133 --> 00:16:27,367
You knew about this!
Why didn't you stop him?!

372
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:29,267
It was too late
when I found out!

373
00:16:29,267 --> 00:16:32,967
- But you still didn't tell me!
- There was nothing I could do.

374
00:16:32,967 --> 00:16:35,067
[RUDY] Don't get mad at Dante.

375
00:16:35,067 --> 00:16:38,033
I asked him
not to tell you and Gabo.

376
00:16:38,033 --> 00:16:40,667
It's just that I feel useless
in this house.

377
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:43,067
You should've thought
about yourself!

378
00:16:43,733 --> 00:16:47,267
If that wound worsens,
that'll be a bigger expense!

379
00:16:47,267 --> 00:16:49,667
Maybe you're just using that
as an excuse to gamble again!

380
00:16:49,667 --> 00:16:51,033
No, son, no.

381
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,100
That's not true.

382
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,533
This is the problem with you.

383
00:16:57,267 --> 00:16:59,267
You saw how hard I worked
for that money.

384
00:17:00,233 --> 00:17:01,533
But you just used it to gamble?!

385
00:17:04,233 --> 00:17:07,600
Sometimes, Mister Rudy's
strategies just don't work.

386
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:10,167
Gabo has a point.

387
00:17:10,167 --> 00:17:11,933
Anyone would get mad
at that situation.

388
00:17:11,933 --> 00:17:14,633
But Mister Rudy
is still his father.

389
00:17:14,633 --> 00:17:15,900
He wouldn't get that mad at him.

390
00:17:15,933 --> 00:17:17,667
He's even letting Miss Betchay
off the hook.

391
00:17:17,667 --> 00:17:20,967
[BINOY] No, but you'll still get
frustrated if that happens.

392
00:17:20,967 --> 00:17:24,300
But, you know,
we also can't blame Mister Rudy.

393
00:17:25,267 --> 00:17:27,100
Especially for people like us.

394
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:30,433
Instantly getting rich
is a huge temptation.

395
00:17:30,433 --> 00:17:33,167
With just one piece of luck,
you can change your life.

396
00:17:33,667 --> 00:17:38,100
But, Bong, gambling should
just be a pastime.

397
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:41,700
Money you're supposed
to use for food and medicine...

398
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:43,333
You shouldn't use that
in gambling.

399
00:17:43,333 --> 00:17:45,067
[IPE] That's enough. Remember...

400
00:17:45,633 --> 00:17:48,033
Not everyone
who hopes, wins.

401
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:50,267
Most of the time,
they just sink further down.

402
00:17:52,367 --> 00:17:53,533
This is the problem with you.

403
00:17:54,367 --> 00:17:56,633
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

404
00:17:56,633 --> 00:17:59,433
[MONEY RUSTLING]

405
00:18:03,633 --> 00:18:04,600
Here.

406
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:06,433
Buy your medicine.

407
00:18:07,333 --> 00:18:09,300
Your wound may
end up getting worse.

408
00:18:11,067 --> 00:18:13,300
[MONEY RUSTLING]

409
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:14,967
Auntie.

410
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:17,467
Have the roof fixed
by tomorrow.

411
00:18:17,467 --> 00:18:18,667
Thank you, Gabo.

412
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,033
Hey, Rudy.

413
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:23,300
Give me that
four thousand pesos.

414
00:18:23,833 --> 00:18:28,067
Give it. I'll just ask someone
to buy your medicine.

415
00:18:28,067 --> 00:18:30,133
- Dante, come on.
- I'll come with you.

416
00:18:32,433 --> 00:18:39,733
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

417
00:18:43,033 --> 00:18:44,300
Son, I'm sorry.

418
00:18:47,233 --> 00:18:48,400
I'm sorry.

419
00:18:49,433 --> 00:18:51,267
[MAMENG] Tekla!
Tekla, my dear.

420
00:18:51,267 --> 00:18:53,233
- [TEKLA] Why, Miss Mameng?
- [MAMENG] Come here.

421
00:18:54,033 --> 00:18:56,333
- Can I ask for your help?
- Of course!

422
00:18:56,367 --> 00:18:58,767
Can you check if any pharmacy
is still open?

423
00:18:58,767 --> 00:19:01,867
Rudy badly needs
his medication.

424
00:19:01,867 --> 00:19:03,300
Of course, Miss Mameng!

425
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:05,100
When it comes to you,
we're even shaking.

426
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,733
- We'll take care of it.
- [MAMENG] Alright.

427
00:19:06,733 --> 00:19:08,467
- We'll be back right away.
- Alright.

428
00:19:08,467 --> 00:19:09,700
- We'll get going.
- Be careful.

429
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:11,533
- Be careful!
- Yeah.

430
00:19:11,533 --> 00:19:13,133
- Be careful.
- Do we go with them?

431
00:19:13,133 --> 00:19:14,667
- Come with us!
- Come with us.

432
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:20,800
Oh, ma'am, my gosh!
It's so hot in the sauna!

433
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:26,300
But the massage was the best!
The tea's even unlimited!

434
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:29,700
- We kept going back for it!
- So long as there's no Q and A.

435
00:19:30,567 --> 00:19:35,300
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

436
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:36,700
- Hi, Mom.
- Oh!

437
00:19:37,567 --> 00:19:38,700
Hi.

438
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:43,833
What's wrong?
You look worried.

439
00:19:43,833 --> 00:19:44,767
[ISOBEL SIGHS]

440
00:19:45,900 --> 00:19:48,067
I'm just worried about Sam.

441
00:19:48,767 --> 00:19:52,800
The NCIA investigated her today.

442
00:19:54,567 --> 00:19:57,533
- She could be dismissed.
- You know, Mom...

443
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:01,333
If only she knows how
to follow the protocol!

444
00:20:01,333 --> 00:20:03,900
As a law enforcer,
she shouldn't have done that!

445
00:20:03,933 --> 00:20:05,800
This is already a big problem
for your sister,

446
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,800
and that's what you decided
to say?

447
00:20:09,433 --> 00:20:10,433
[GLASS THUDS]

448
00:20:11,167 --> 00:20:12,533
In our line of work, Ma,

449
00:20:12,533 --> 00:20:14,600
all of our actions
have consequences.

450
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:17,667
It's either a reward
or a punishment.

451
00:20:19,333 --> 00:20:20,800
I'm just being honest.

452
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:27,433
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

453
00:20:27,433 --> 00:20:34,400
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

454
00:20:38,467 --> 00:20:40,533
[ENGINE REVVING]

455
00:20:40,533 --> 00:20:43,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

456
00:20:43,967 --> 00:20:46,500
[ENGINE REVVING]

457
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:49,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

458
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

459
00:20:56,667 --> 00:20:58,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

460
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:06,267
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

461
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,333
There! Catch her!

462
00:21:11,333 --> 00:21:16,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

463
00:21:17,733 --> 00:21:23,367
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

464
00:21:24,167 --> 00:21:26,233
I'm sorry I spent the...

465
00:21:27,367 --> 00:21:29,233
the money you gave me.

466
00:21:30,833 --> 00:21:32,233
I'm really sorry.

467
00:21:38,167 --> 00:21:40,567
You know
how difficult life is, Pa.

468
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:47,333
You should know to...

469
00:21:48,933 --> 00:21:51,600
avoid doing the things
you know are bad.

470
00:21:53,867 --> 00:21:55,533
You just had surgery.

471
00:21:57,633 --> 00:21:59,600
Do you know how risky
your situation is right now?

472
00:22:01,467 --> 00:22:02,667
What if you get infected?

473
00:22:03,433 --> 00:22:04,567
What if you die?

474
00:22:06,567 --> 00:22:08,767
You know how important
you are to me.

475
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:14,333
I know that, son.

476
00:22:15,633 --> 00:22:17,400
This is all my fault.

477
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:19,633
I shouldn't have been careless.

478
00:22:20,667 --> 00:22:22,467
If I just worked hard,

479
00:22:23,267 --> 00:22:24,933
and didn't rely on luck,

480
00:22:26,733 --> 00:22:28,867
you would've had a better life.

481
00:22:31,967 --> 00:22:33,867
We wouldn't have lost your mom.

482
00:22:35,233 --> 00:22:36,633
That's the problem, Pa.

483
00:22:37,967 --> 00:22:39,767
You know Mama is gone.

484
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,867
You should take better care
of yourself.

485
00:22:45,433 --> 00:22:48,200
You're the most important
person in my life right now.

486
00:22:49,533 --> 00:22:52,000
I don't know what to do
if something bad happens to you.

487
00:22:55,033 --> 00:22:56,967
I'm not mad about the money.

488
00:22:57,667 --> 00:23:00,267
I'm mad that you're not
taking care of yourself.

489
00:23:05,633 --> 00:23:07,500
I'm really sorry, son.

490
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:09,800
You know...

491
00:23:10,933 --> 00:23:13,267
I'm so lucky

492
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,900
to have a son like you.

493
00:23:18,533 --> 00:23:21,567
I bet your future wife
will be lucky, too.

494
00:23:23,667 --> 00:23:25,600
Because I'm sure

495
00:23:26,067 --> 00:23:28,633
that you're going to take care
of your family.

496
00:23:30,333 --> 00:23:32,033
You will be a loving father

497
00:23:33,567 --> 00:23:35,533
and do everything for them.

498
00:23:35,533 --> 00:23:38,733
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

499
00:23:38,733 --> 00:23:41,567
[YOUNG GABO]
<i> I love you, Mommy and Daddy.</i>

500
00:23:41,567 --> 00:23:44,033
- [BELINDA]<i> We love you.
</i>- [RUDY] We love you, Gabriel.

501
00:23:44,033 --> 00:23:45,567
- [YOUNG GABO]<i> Mommy?
</i>- [BELINDA] Mm?

502
00:23:45,567 --> 00:23:47,800
[YOUNG GABO]
<i> What did you pray for?</i>

503
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:51,333
[BELINDA]<i> I was just thanking
</i> Him for all the blessings.

504
00:23:51,700 --> 00:23:54,867
<i> For your Daddy, for you,</i>

505
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:57,100
for the food we have every day,

506
00:23:57,100 --> 00:23:58,433
<i> for our home,</i>

507
00:23:58,433 --> 00:24:02,500
and of course, for all the time
<i> we spend together.</i>

508
00:24:11,667 --> 00:24:13,467
I'm really sorry, son.

509
00:24:13,767 --> 00:24:16,667
F-for what I did.

510
00:24:19,767 --> 00:24:21,733
I'm sorry, too, Pa.

511
00:24:24,867 --> 00:24:26,400
I hope you forgive me.

512
00:24:27,767 --> 00:24:34,733
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

513
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:58,733
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

514
00:25:14,767 --> 00:25:18,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

515
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:20,933
[GUNSHOTS]

516
00:25:23,767 --> 00:25:25,433
This woman is tough!

517
00:25:26,067 --> 00:25:27,933
Don't let her get away!

518
00:25:28,767 --> 00:25:35,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

519
00:25:41,433 --> 00:25:42,667
Where is she?

520
00:25:42,667 --> 00:25:45,100
Let's split up!

521
00:25:50,133 --> 00:25:57,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

522
00:26:04,833 --> 00:26:06,700
We got you now, Jacinto!

523
00:26:06,700 --> 00:26:07,767
[GUNSHOTS]

524
00:26:09,233 --> 00:26:10,700
[WATER SPLASHES]

525
00:26:12,567 --> 00:26:13,667
[DOOR OPENS]

526
00:26:13,667 --> 00:26:14,833
Manny.

527
00:26:14,833 --> 00:26:16,167
[DOOR CLOSES]

528
00:26:16,167 --> 00:26:19,133
The TRO they secured
for Ginintuang Lupa...

529
00:26:19,867 --> 00:26:21,167
Have you taken care of it?

530
00:26:21,167 --> 00:26:23,000
I have talked
to the person we know.

531
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:24,533
They're already working
on a way

532
00:26:24,533 --> 00:26:25,967
to push through
with the demolition.

533
00:26:25,967 --> 00:26:27,667
Well, that's not enough, Manny.

534
00:26:27,667 --> 00:26:29,133
I need results.

535
00:26:29,133 --> 00:26:32,700
We're wasting time and
money while my land sits idle.

536
00:26:32,700 --> 00:26:39,667
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

537
00:26:43,900 --> 00:26:45,033
Coffee, ma'am.

538
00:26:45,033 --> 00:26:46,533
Oh, thank you.

539
00:26:47,667 --> 00:26:48,667
[SOFT THUDS]

540
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,133
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

541
00:26:51,100 --> 00:26:52,767
- Mom.
- Hmm?

542
00:26:52,767 --> 00:26:54,700
Why aren't you asleep yet?
It's late.

543
00:26:57,100 --> 00:26:59,200
Have you heard from Sam?
Any word?

544
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,967
Sam? No.

545
00:27:01,933 --> 00:27:03,567
Ma, Sam isn't a kid anymore.

546
00:27:04,233 --> 00:27:06,867
She probably went to
have drinks with her colleagues

547
00:27:06,867 --> 00:27:09,267
to reduce their anxiety.

548
00:27:09,267 --> 00:27:11,233
But she doesn't do this.

549
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:15,200
Whenever she has something
to do, she calls to let me know.

550
00:27:15,900 --> 00:27:18,067
She hasn't been in touch
since this morning,

551
00:27:18,067 --> 00:27:21,033
so I don't know
what happened to her.

552
00:27:21,033 --> 00:27:23,267
The last time she went home,
she was drunk.

553
00:27:24,233 --> 00:27:27,200
Did she inform you?
I noticed that, you see.

554
00:27:27,200 --> 00:27:28,133
She didn't say a word.

555
00:27:28,133 --> 00:27:31,733
So she might be
doing the same right now.

556
00:27:31,733 --> 00:27:35,933
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

557
00:27:35,933 --> 00:27:37,100
Don't worry.

558
00:27:40,233 --> 00:27:41,233
Wait for her.

559
00:27:43,900 --> 00:27:45,233
Better safe than sorry.

560
00:27:45,900 --> 00:27:47,767
That's right.
Let's make sure of it.

561
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:49,867
Okay. Open fire!

562
00:27:50,267 --> 00:27:55,133
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

563
00:27:57,267 --> 00:27:58,600
She's surely dead.

564
00:27:59,167 --> 00:28:00,267
Let's go.

565
00:28:00,267 --> 00:28:07,233
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

566
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:10,900
[WATER SPLASHES]

567
00:28:25,967 --> 00:28:29,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

568
00:28:29,367 --> 00:28:31,433
She just got hired, and she'll
be promoted as manager already?

569
00:28:31,433 --> 00:28:33,667
<i>He knew that I wasn't happy
about Betchay</i>

570
00:28:33,667 --> 00:28:35,300
<i> working in BeerGin.</i>

571
00:28:35,300 --> 00:28:36,800
<i>And now he's even
promoting her?!</i>

572
00:28:37,367 --> 00:28:39,300
<i> This isn't an ordinary ambush.</i>

573
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:41,467
<i> The Zafras are getting back
at the NCIA.</i>

574
00:28:41,467 --> 00:28:44,200
<i>No one is declared dead
if you didn't find a body.</i>

575
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:46,167
<i> And Sam is their target.</i>

576
00:28:46,167 --> 00:28:49,467
<i>Don't go home unless you've
confirmed that she's dead.</i>

577
00:28:49,467 --> 00:28:51,700
<i>Admit that your family
is involved.</i>

578
00:28:51,700 --> 00:28:54,800
<i>We're talking about the life
of my agent here!</i>

579
00:28:54,800 --> 00:28:57,133
<i>If your agents
are getting killed,</i>

580
00:28:57,167 --> 00:28:58,533
<i>don't try to pin the blame
on others!</i>

581
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:00,200
<i> You're outsiders.</i>

582
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:02,333
<i> I'm the king of Tondo.</i>

583
00:29:02,333 --> 00:29:04,700
<i> Anyone who wants to enter
has to go through me.</i>

584
00:29:08,667 --> 00:29:10,467
<i> We can kill all of you.</i>

585
00:29:10,467 --> 00:29:11,700
<i> Go on! Shoot me!</i>

586
00:29:12,567 --> 00:29:14,233
<i> I'm ready, Lord.</i>

587
00:29:14,233 --> 00:29:16,233
<i> You can drop her to me
if You want to.</i>

588
00:29:16,233 --> 00:29:17,567
[CRASHING]

589
00:29:17,567 --> 00:29:18,900
<i> Oh! Oh!</i>

590
00:29:18,900 --> 00:29:20,633
[OBJECTS CLATTER]

591
00:29:21,833 --> 00:29:24,800
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]
